   "source": [
    "# Q-Mini — Training-Ready Model Builder (Build now, train later)This notebook prepares one complete **0.7M-class, training-ready Q-Mini package** in Google Drive.It will:- use the repository's from-scratch CausalConv + gated diagonal SSM + sparse Top-1 MoE model;- keep Transformer self-attention and Q/K/V attention out of the architecture;- fit the Hugging Face Tokenizers byte-level BPE tokenizer to the corpus you place in Drive;- create fingerprinted train/validation token streams and the required loss masks;- build the full random-initialized model and export Q2-v2 packed matrix weights;- verify the model, tokenizer, data manifests and Drive copy before publishing the package.**This notebook does not train the neural model.** It does not create an optimizer, run backward passes or update model weights. Tokenizer fitting and dataset preparation are preprocessing, not neural-model training.The default 0.7M-class profile is the Colab training target. The repository's 5B profile can be initialized as a packed artifact by the separate 5B builder, but the current trainer does **not** implement FSDP/ZeRO or 5B multi-GPU training. Do not use a 5B artifact with this single-device training path."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ---------------- USER SETTINGS ----------------MODEL_CONFIG_REL = \"configs/qmini_light_0.7m.json\"DATA_REL = \"QMini/datasets\"ART_REL = \"QMini\"VOCAB_SIZE = 4096VALIDATION_FRACTION = 0.02NEAR_DUPLICATE_HAMMING_DISTANCE = 0LOSS_MASK_MODE = \"auto\"  # auto = assistant-only for chat/Q&A, full LM for plain text# Optional strict dataset-release gate. Supply a qmini-source-provenance-v1 JSON# file in Google Drive before setting RELEASE_MODE=True.SOURCE_METADATA_REL = NoneRELEASE_MODE = False# The builder is build-only. Training is activated separately from# QMini_Training_Runner.ipynb after the model package has been verified.TRAIN_SEQUENCE_LENGTH = 1024print(\"Model profile:\", MODEL_CONFIG_REL)print(\"Neural model training enabled: False (separate runner only)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ---------------- GOOGLE DRIVE + SOURCE CHECKOUT ----------------from google.colab import drivedrive.mount(\"/content/drive\")from pathlib import Pathfrom datetime import datetime, timezoneimport hashlibimport jsonimport mathimport shutilimport subprocessimport sysimport timeMY_DRIVE = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive\")if not MY_DRIVE.is_dir():    raise RuntimeError(\"Google Drive is not mounted at /content/drive/MyDrive.\")DATA_DIR = MY_DRIVE / DATA_RELART_ROOT = MY_DRIVE / ART_RELDATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)ART_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)REPO_DIR = Path(\"/content/Q-Mini-Light-0.7M-Training-Ready\")REPOSITORY_URL = \"https://github.com/lion36508/Q-mini-light-0.7M.git\"def run_checked(command, *, cwd=None, capture_output=False):    command = [str(part) for part in command]    print(\"$\", \" \".join(command))    return subprocess.run(        command,        cwd=str(cwd) if cwd else None,        check=True,        text=True,        capture_output=capture_output,    )if REPO_DIR.exists():    run_checked([\"git\", \"fetch\", \"--depth\", \"1\", \"origin\", \"main\"], cwd=REPO_DIR)    run_checked([\"git\", \"reset\", \"--hard\", \"origin/main\"], cwd=REPO_DIR)else:    run_checked([\"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth\", \"1\", \"--branch\", \"main\", REPOSITORY_URL, REPO_DIR])SOURCE_REVISION = run_checked(    [\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], cwd=REPO_DIR, capture_output=True).stdout.strip()MODEL_CONFIG_PATH = REPO_DIR / MODEL_CONFIG_RELif not MODEL_CONFIG_PATH.is_file():    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Model config not found: {MODEL_CONFIG_PATH}\")print(\"Source revision:\", SOURCE_REVISION)print(\"Corpus folder:\", DATA_DIR)print(\"Drive artifact root:\", ART_ROOT)"
   ]
  },
