    "## Separate build and training lifecycleThe builder is build-only. It does not create an optimizer, run backward passes, or update model weights. The completed Drive package contains the initial Q2-v2 model, matching tokenizer and prepared streams, plus a checksum-verified copy of the Q-Mini training source in `training_runtime/`. That runtime is marked `enabled: false`.Training starts only from the separate [QMini Training Runner](https://colab.research.google.com/github/lion36508/Q-Mini/blob/main/colab/QMini_Training_Runner.ipynb). Its checkpoint store updates one visible `training_progress.json` record, keeps two verified recovery generations, and restores the newest valid checkpoint after a runtime/server interruption.Q2-v2 stores matrix symbols at 2 bits; row scales are FP32, vector parameters FP16, and the current QAT training master weights and AdamW optimizer state are FP32. The current single-device trainer supports the 0.7M-class research configuration, not 5B distributed training. A future FSDP/ZeRO backend can be replaced independently without changing the model artifact format."
